----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Set = Unique items collection in Python!
Best for finding duplicates, comparing server lists & tracking unique values! 🚀
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🤔 What is Set?
Think of Set as a Bag of Unique Items 🎒

Normal List:
['web1', 'web2', 'web1', 'web3', 'web2']
 Duplicates allowed!

Set:
{'web1', 'web2', 'web3'}
 Duplicates automatically removed!

# Set uses { } curly brackets
# But NO key:value like dictionary

servers = {'web1', 'web2', 'web3'}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Create Set

# Create set directly
servers = {'web1', 'web2', 'web3'}

# Create from list (removes duplicates!)
server_list = ['web1', 'web2', 'web1', 'web3', 'web2']
servers = set(server_list)
print(servers)   # {'web1', 'web2', 'web3'}

# Empty set
empty = set()    # NOT {} - that makes dictionary!

# Set with numbers
ports = {80, 443, 8080, 22}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Duplicates Automatically Removed

# This is the MAIN feature of Set!

# List - keeps duplicates
logs = ['ERROR', 'INFO', 'ERROR', 'WARNING', 'ERROR', 'INFO']
print(logs)
# ['ERROR', 'INFO', 'ERROR', 'WARNING', 'ERROR', 'INFO']

# Set - removes duplicates automatically!
unique_logs = set(logs)
print(unique_logs)
# {'ERROR', 'INFO', 'WARNING'}

# Real DevOps use - find unique IPs from logs
ip_logs = [
    '192.168.1.1',
    '192.168.1.2',
    '192.168.1.1',
    '192.168.1.3',
    '192.168.1.2',
    '192.168.1.1'
]

unique_ips = set(ip_logs)
print(unique_ips)
# {'192.168.1.1', '192.168.1.2', '192.168.1.3'}
print(f"Unique IPs: {len(unique_ips)}")   # 3
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Add & Remove Items

servers = {'web1', 'web2', 'web3'}

# Add item
servers.add('web4')
print(servers)   # {'web1', 'web2', 'web3', 'web4'}

# Add duplicate - ignored automatically!
servers.add('web1')
print(servers)   # {'web1', 'web2', 'web3', 'web4'}
# web1 not added again!

# Remove item
servers.remove('web1')      # Error if not found!
print(servers)

# Safe remove - no error if not found
servers.discard('web99')    # No error!
servers.discard('web2')     # Removed safely
print(servers)

# Remove and return random item
item = servers.pop()
print(f"Removed: {item}")

# Clear all
servers.clear()
print(servers)   # set()
